From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:47:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: no fault snapshot before the device is registered

With the MDP clock kept, the bootloader's splash still scans out when
msm attaches its IOMMU domain, and can fault before the splash is mapped
into it. The snapshot that queues then duplicates CRTC states that don't
exist yet: a NULL dereference in dpu_crtc_duplicate_state, in the
snapshot worker, with the modeset locks held, and the boot hangs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
index e5d0ea629448..40cce35a85ce 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
@@ -169,6 +169,13 @@ static int msm_kms_fault_handler(void *arg, unsigned long iova, int flags, void
 {
 	struct msm_kms *kms = arg;
 
+	/*
+	 * A fault can come as soon as the domain is attached: the bootloader's
+	 * splash, still scanning out, before msm has any CRTC state to snapshot
+	 */
+	if (!kms->dev->registered)
+		return -ENOSYS;
+
 	if (atomic_read(&kms->fault_snapshot_capture) == 0) {
 		msm_disp_snapshot_state(kms->dev);
 		atomic_inc(&kms->fault_snapshot_capture);
